BloodHound trust-edge schema compatibility fix

Why this change is required:
- SpecterOps BloodHound v7.4 removed the legacy TrustedBy edge.
- Current structural trust edges are SameForestTrust and CrossForestTrust.
- Structural trust edges are non-traversable and must not be treated as attack-path hops.
- Traversable trust abuse is represented by SpoofSIDHistory and AbuseTGTDelegation.
- The target ORI environment runs BloodHound CE 9.1.0, so TrustedBy queries return no current trust relationships.

Implementation:
- Updated bloodhound://cypher/reference relationship guidance.
- Updated bloodhound://guides/ad and bloodhound://guides/ad-methodology.
- Updated bloodhound://cypher/offensive-queries.
- Updated the bloodhound_assistant system prompt.
- Structural inventory queries now use SameForestTrust|CrossForestTrust.
- Shortest-path allowlists now use SpoofSIDHistory|AbuseTGTDelegation.
- Added README compatibility guidance with official SpecterOps references.
- Added regression tests covering every affected resource and prompt surface.

Validation:
- Focused suite: 169 passed.
- Full suite: 350 passed, 11 skipped.
- git diff --check passed.
- No live BloodHound writes or uploads were performed.

